I have a workaround for this. Put `[disabled]="selectFixBool"` on your `<select>` element. `selectFixBool` is a boolean declared at the top of your component. Then assign `true` to it in the constructor of your component.

```
constructor () {
  // Other stuff.
  this.selectFixBool = true;
}
```

During `ngOnInit` you immediately switch it to `false` using `setTimeout()` (which enables the select control). Like this:

```
public ngOnInit() {
  // Small hack to fix select option bug for IE/Edge (see #10010)
  setTimeout(
    () => {
      this.selectFixBool = false;
    }
  );
}
```

I don't know why, but it works for me. I'm using angular `2.0.0-rc.6` right now.

**update** this workaround doesn't work on Edge
